  :seon.task/plan "What was seen, in the lab, 2026-11-04: a render's var call whose contract does not ask for :seon.ctx/ctx or :seon.db/db (seon.render/inputs) is kept as a call by seon.render/emit, with no error: an agent's new part printed as `[#'lab.ui/where {} 7751]`. A trap once every agent writes renders. Tried in this form, any var call as a component: one line, but drawing-one-list-costs-that-list-not-the-page goes from 616 to 1,563 calls, each seon.render/hiccup becoming a component, and the kept call the model reads as structure is gone. So not that. What should be true: the rule that tells a component from a kept call is stated by data, and the call an agent meant as a part says why it stayed a call. The lab settles which."
