or-byte proof of the request is green through this walk on both worlds (175 tests in wire, render, render-cost and ctx); example sessions go through render-pull with a root call; a model render's opts carry :seon.render/index. Next: land the two branches together after the config entity (Optimization's erase window), then step (5)'s deletions with 2b's (show-page!, the stored page evals, :wire readers), then (6)-(7). State 2026-11-10 (Web, jolt/walk-2a): main merged in; Context's 10f0e428b2 taken (a model render's opts carry :seon.render/index); the model render's schema property is :seon.render/openai-compat and the model output's reader seon.render/openai-compat (was wire-of), agreed with Context so 2b renames none of the interface; the 2a proof red with the model render disabled (4 assertions), green with it. Step (6) built: seon.render.ui/agent-parts (was task-list), a render of the agent's pull with its :seon.ctx/pattern as var metadata, what a turn's diff compares (Context's stand-in goes at 2b's merge). The owner's order (2026-11-10): the config entity (jolt/config-entity, on the erase window) lands first, then 2a whole with the best match; a split without it is kept unlanded on jolt/walk-2a-split. Left: (7a) renders for a cite, a doc section, a search, a result and a var with its verdict, the cite's after the erase window's :seon.cite/target, designed with Context since the model reads them; (7b) the four second renders merged, with Context where the model reads them; (7c) the layouts and layout-of deleted, with 2b's openai-compat renders, since the conversation reaches the model through conversation-list's :wire marks until then."
